o divide by $2$, we split the whole into $2$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/c7/c7a402dc351163f8044557fd8fe73fe68b7af594284e92efc5115fde0017c7e2.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{4}{14}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{7}÷2=\\frac{4}{14}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142944 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "46548510-66c1-542c-8a7b-a80d55247aa7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Divisor From a Division Model"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e4adc2c-1985-5645-bb66-c0a09ee8de75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433846} {:answer/id #uuid "733ce884-d9fa-57ea-b302-23a3a4fcc7ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433861} {:answer/id #uuid "805979da-0872-5d4a-a69d-a023ca171302" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433866} {:answer/id #uuid "8e883dad-7c79-57fe-9969-050966ee92b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433874} {:answer/id #uuid "cc5e07f2-a4f4-5eda-acd7-5f8f3c974d14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e4adc2c-1985-5645-bb66-c0a09ee8de75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433846} :answer-field/id #uuid "38a44da7-0543-5023-aea9-074c4f6b3e92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433912}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "175f029d-3a5f-53c9-899b-6473231cb987" :question/math-academy-id "q-61231" :question/problem "![](images/17/177011333d5e29ed699884a665aa58aea43eec52b64d045daa5370a71e9f2a96.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the division problem above?" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{4}{7}$ on the left and $\\frac{4}{14}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/9a/9a2f2136b843a54c3038b2905570d1932b2547279953093f3b6c89fc65d4b11b.png)\n\nThe division operation splits each vertical line into $2$ equal parts. So the shaded parts on the left are $2$ times larger than the shaded parts on the right.  \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{7}÷2=\\frac{4}{14}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433941 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142944 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "46548510-66c1-542c-8a7b-a80d55247aa7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Divisor From a Division Model"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fb4e8db-9998-5cf9-a525-4bcb8a827f22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433838} {:answer/id #uuid "25b034c3-244b-5296-91f1-65762c4ed0ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433840} {:answer/id #uuid "354fb067-7ac0-5d96-ae02-d004124cf746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433844} {:answer/id #uuid "440c40eb-0100-5cd9-8768-bd9c776c8725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433847} {:answer/id #uuid "f1478a8c-f482-50b5-ae24-9659a16e71c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25b034c3-244b-5296-91f1-65762c4ed0ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433840} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e336f67-24e1-5ca1-81fc-13e9fcdc7100" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7851f4de-9f18-5ad9-a23b-706dffcb0f10" :question/math-academy-id "q-61232" :question/problem "![](images/07/07a813ac4f544d1dbad9afe89ebaa772eefe8a41dc1cf8be481843cc2d7defbc.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the division problem above?" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{5}{8}$ on the left and $\\frac{5}{24}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/67/67dd516958b830c5442ab740683b23866c09e9422ac48c9259131f73870ae951.png)\n\nThe division operation splits each vertical line into $3$ equal parts. So the shaded parts on the left are $3$ times larger than the shaded parts on the right.  \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{8}÷3=\\frac{5}{24}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186143542 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142944 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "46548510-66c1-542c-8a7b-a80d55247aa7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Divisor From a Division Model"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f362cef5-36f6-5be2-8b76-185ee585d864" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186142222} {:answer/id #uuid "25faedad-75f4-5b6c-af61-2ae16afbede6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186142223} {:answer/id #uuid "3d8175f4-46d5-5a4f-ace0-b371f5ccecb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186142224} {:answer/id #uuid "66cef24c-fa4a-51e9-83d0-fbab99329af2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186142225} {:answer/id #uuid "6f10fb1d-0bd0-5303-8b0e-18c93ae6efec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186142226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25faedad-75f4-5b6c-af61-2ae16afbede6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186142223} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a0177f3-2406-5fa8-8bf1-fc9160374224" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186142221}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1f89fb8d-4b5b-5292-a64a-e181392d9a34" :question/math-academy-id "q-61234" :question/problem "![](images/1b/1bdaebd241576e9101a30d6b8882950494220a2f06f9fdbe1e357107fafabe9e.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the division problem above?" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{2}{3}$ on the left and $\\frac{2}{12}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/6f/6f6687c4190a54e9974dc600ced3a2662718cce1bcd5d49410a994259ac06e58.png)\n\nThe division operation splits each vertical line into $4$ equal parts. So the shaded parts on the left are $4$ times larger than the shaded parts on the right. \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}÷4=\\frac{2}{12}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $4.$"}]}
